Appendix C: Layer Interaction Analysis and Known Interference Points

---

C.1 Motivation

Seven layers operating concurrently may interact synergistically or antagonistically. Identifying boundary failure modes is essential for principled composition.

C.2 Synergistic Interactions

· L1 ↔ L6: ASIDE eliminates data‑sourced instruction nodes; AgentArmor’s PDG type checker trivially passes. Layer 6 is a redundant backstop for Layer 1 failures—defense‑in‑depth.
· L5 ↔ L6: DRIFT masks injected memory before context insertion; unmasked payloads are caught by AgentArmor’s data‑flow type check. Independent checkpoints.
· L2 ↔ L4: ATTP’s signing provides cryptographic identity ground truth for ZTAA policy evaluation. Layers must be deployed together; neither is operationally useful alone.

C.3 Antagonistic Interactions

· L3 ↔ L6 (Cascade Failure Risk): If VIGIL blocks a tool output, AgentArmor receives an incomplete trace with missing observation node. This may cause a false security violation or an incomplete graph. Explicit error‑propagation semantics between L3 and L6 are not yet specified.
· L1 ↔ L3 (Redundant Latency): PCFI processes every tool output at the API gateway; TOF independently applies schema enforcement and VIGIL. In high‑throughput systems, double processing consumes latency budget. Consolidation may be needed in Phase 2.
· L5 ↔ L1 (Temporal Gap): Memory entries written before IDSL deployment were not protected by ASIDE/PCFI. Later recall bypasses IDSL because the entry enters context as a recalled memory, not a new tool output. A‑MemGuard partially mitigates via dual‑memory lessons but does not retroactively sanitize historical entries. A deployment‑time memory audit is required.
· L7 ↔ GDPR (Auditability vs. Minimization): Immutable logs contain personal data (financial, health, communications). Full reconstructability conflicts with GDPR Article 5(1)(c) (data minimisation). A privacy‑preserving audit architecture with selective encryption and DPO‑controlled key escrow is needed; currently not specified.

