D.3 Composed Framework Evaluation Protocol

1. Baseline: Measure undefended $\Pi_{\text{benign}}^{\text{base}}$ and $\Pi_{\text{attack}}^{\text{base}}$.
2. Incremental activation: Activate layers in order 1 → 3 → 5 → 6 → 2 → 4 → 7, recording marginal benefit and capability cost.
3. Cascade interaction testing: For each adjacent pair $(L_i, L_{i+1})$, test boundary interactions identified in Appendix C.3. Specify expected behavior.
4. Adaptive attack evaluation: Subject composed framework to $\mathcal{A}_W$‑class adversary (human red‑teaming or AgentVigil). Report residual ASR separately from static ASR.
5. Capability preservation check: Verify $\Pi_{\text{benign}}^D \ge 0.95 \cdot \Pi_{\text{benign}}^{\text{base}}$ on all three benchmarks. If violated, identify responsible layers and redesign.

